WEBVTT

00:02.300 --> 00:04.790
<i>I worked as a salaryman 
for a toxic company,</i>

00:04.790 --> 00:06.580
<i>until I reincarnated...</i>

00:06.580 --> 00:10.640
<i>in a crazy world where everything is 
dropped by monsters in dungeons.</i>

00:11.000 --> 00:15.410
<i>In my new life, I'm level 1, 
but I have a unique skill</i>

00:15.410 --> 00:17.750
<i>that puts all of my drop rates at rank S.</i>

00:18.080 --> 00:21.630
<i>And today, I'm moving... 
for the second time!</i>

00:21.630 --> 00:23.000
<i>And then...</i>

00:23.000 --> 00:25.180
<i>What?! A metallic me?!</i>

00:25.180 --> 00:27.440
<i>And I meet yet another new girl...</i>

00:27.440 --> 00:29.440
<i>What the heck is gonna happen this time?!</i>

00:36.140 --> 00:45.270
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

02:00.010 --> 02:05.020
<b>The Arrival of Alice</b>

02:12.930 --> 02:15.470
Good morning, Yoda.

02:16.030 --> 02:17.940
Morning...

02:17.940 --> 02:18.940
Huh?

02:18.940 --> 02:21.240
Celeste?! What happened?!

02:21.950 --> 02:23.150
Good morning...

02:23.150 --> 02:25.470
She says her head hurts.

02:25.470 --> 02:28.070
A headache? Did you catch a cold?

02:28.070 --> 02:31.000
No. It's a magic storm.

02:31.000 --> 02:32.710
A magic storm?

02:32.710 --> 02:36.210
The natural phenomenon that 
prevents people from using magic?

02:36.770 --> 02:38.610
Whenever there's a magic storm,

02:38.610 --> 02:41.430
my head throbs with pain and feels heavy.

02:41.430 --> 02:45.470
The storms make some 
magic users feel that bad?

02:45.830 --> 02:48.530
I'll be fine as long as
 I just carry on normally.

02:48.530 --> 02:50.890
After the storm passes, I'll feel better.

02:51.240 --> 02:54.240
Well, then, instead of going 
back to the dungeon today,

02:54.240 --> 02:55.870
let's go look at bigger houses.

02:56.220 --> 03:00.520
<i>Yeah... One big enough that she won't 
feel sick during magic storms.</i>

03:00.800 --> 03:04.050
<i>Are there any houses that can soften 
the effects of a magic storm?</i>

03:05.220 --> 03:11.290
This is the only property I have today 
that meets all of your criteria.

03:15.290 --> 03:17.720
My headache's cleared up!

03:17.720 --> 03:18.960
Really?

03:18.960 --> 03:22.220
Yes! I didn't know there were 
houses that had such effects!

03:22.490 --> 03:28.130
This property was built using the latest 
magic storm-blocking construction methods,

03:28.130 --> 03:32.220
which should be very reassuring 
for any magic user.

03:34.140 --> 03:36.560
The kitchen is its own 
room, and it's so big!

03:36.560 --> 03:38.160
What do you think?

03:38.160 --> 03:39.500
It's fantastic!

03:39.850 --> 03:42.150
How much does this cost per month?

03:42.150 --> 03:45.480
Since it was built with all 
the latest technology,

03:45.480 --> 03:48.080
the rent is considerably 
higher than market price.

03:48.520 --> 03:50.340
It's 400,000 pilos.

03:50.340 --> 03:52.400
400,000 pilos?!

03:52.400 --> 03:55.330
Not a problem. We'll take it.

03:55.330 --> 03:58.840
Wait, Ryota! We couldn't...

03:58.840 --> 03:59.740
It's fine.

04:00.040 --> 04:03.190
"A house where Celeste and 
Emily can always smile"

04:03.190 --> 04:06.680
was at the top of my list of 
criteria for our new house.

04:05.700 --> 04:06.680
Rabbit...

04:06.680 --> 04:10.470
Besides, when I saw how 
much better you feel now,

04:10.470 --> 04:13.370
I couldn't even think 
about any other options.

04:14.380 --> 04:17.270
Well, let's start moving in!

04:24.180 --> 04:26.840
Seems like the magic storm's over.

04:26.840 --> 04:28.860
Yes, and aside from that...

04:35.260 --> 04:38.810
Emily's a force to be reckoned with. 
All this in one day!

04:38.810 --> 04:42.300
You said it. Emily really is amazing.

04:42.300 --> 04:43.690
What shall we do today?

04:43.690 --> 04:45.040
Carrot!

04:45.430 --> 04:47.580
The harvest festival's coming up soon.

04:47.580 --> 04:51.790
I think we should follow the list of
 high-priced items Erza gave me

04:51.790 --> 04:55.210
and look for rare monsters 
on level 7 of Telulu.

04:56.090 --> 04:57.360
Carrot...

04:57.590 --> 05:00.650
Yeah, we'll get some carrots 
while we're at it.

05:01.640 --> 05:02.950
Forgiven!

05:03.290 --> 05:05.550
Breakfast is ready!

05:05.550 --> 05:10.740
All right! Let's eat a delicious meal
 so we can give our all today!

05:10.740 --> 05:11.480
Yes!

05:11.480 --> 05:12.820
Absolutely!

05:12.820 --> 05:14.340
Carrot!

05:14.910 --> 05:19.460
<b>Telulu Level 7</b>

05:18.470 --> 05:19.450
Snow?

05:19.450 --> 05:21.490
Inside a dungeon?

05:21.490 --> 05:23.230
It's dungeon snow.

05:23.230 --> 05:27.070
Depending on how they're made, 
some dungeons have floors where it can snow.

05:27.070 --> 05:28.390
I see...

05:31.110 --> 05:33.470
You always seem to have 
all the info, Celeste.

05:33.470 --> 05:36.330
Huh? I-I wouldn't say that...

05:36.330 --> 05:38.180
Yay! He praised me!

05:47.270 --> 05:48.720
Well done!

05:48.720 --> 05:52.200
I am intensely moved right now!

05:52.650 --> 05:53.910
Captain...

05:53.910 --> 05:57.190
It was so hard, wasn't it? 
You suffered so much!

05:57.190 --> 05:59.100
I know all about it!

05:59.840 --> 06:01.980
I feel the same way!

06:01.980 --> 06:04.690
Every time you two felt pain,

06:04.690 --> 06:07.170
I felt it right along with you!

06:07.170 --> 06:09.510
You were suffering, too, Captain?

06:09.840 --> 06:11.920
I don't matter one bit!

06:12.190 --> 06:16.390
You two endured the stress 
and grew stronger for it!

06:16.390 --> 06:18.350
I'm proud of you!

06:18.350 --> 06:21.420
Captain! The same goes for us!

06:21.420 --> 06:24.080
We're so glad we followed you!

06:24.080 --> 06:25.770
<i>Their brainwashing's complete.</i>

06:26.800 --> 06:28.190
Yoda?

06:28.440 --> 06:30.380
Nothing. Let's go.

06:32.850 --> 06:35.460
Yoda! There's a monster!

06:48.260 --> 06:49.560
What in the world—

06:50.390 --> 06:52.080
Stop, Ryota!

06:52.080 --> 06:54.520
You can't defeat a guts slime alone!

06:54.520 --> 06:55.590
What do you mean?

06:55.970 --> 06:59.580
Guts slimes become invincible 
when near death,

06:59.580 --> 07:03.270
and they no longer take damage from 
the last person to attack them.

07:03.270 --> 07:06.410
So we need someone to weaken it 
and someone to finish it off?

07:06.410 --> 07:07.260
Yes!

07:11.660 --> 07:13.920
Wow! You beat it!

07:13.920 --> 07:17.510
Solo-proof floors. Not very common.

07:17.510 --> 07:20.110
You can leave this floor to us.

07:20.110 --> 07:22.580
Ryota is the best one to finish them off.

07:29.200 --> 07:30.810
Finish it off!

07:33.930 --> 07:35.850
We did it!

07:35.850 --> 07:39.690
Yeah. They're not that strong 
if we all fight them together.

07:39.690 --> 07:41.060
Onions...

07:41.060 --> 07:43.260
Do you like onions, Eve?

07:43.260 --> 07:45.110
All I need are carrots.

07:45.110 --> 07:47.920
In that case, I'll make curry tonight.

07:47.920 --> 07:52.280
It'll have potatoes, onions, 
and big chunks of carrot in it.

07:52.280 --> 07:54.030
Big chunks of carrot!

07:54.940 --> 07:56.550
Sounds good!

07:56.550 --> 07:57.850
Celeste, do you like curry—

07:57.850 --> 07:58.840
Watch out!

08:00.620 --> 08:01.730
Yoda!

08:01.730 --> 08:02.420
Carrot!

08:02.950 --> 08:06.420
I'm fine. And call me something else!

08:06.840 --> 08:08.750
<i>It's not like the ones we've been fighting.</i>

08:09.060 --> 08:10.650
<i>It must be a rare monster!</i>

08:11.170 --> 08:13.930
Celeste, how do we defeat this one?

08:13.930 --> 08:15.780
A high-guts slime.

08:15.780 --> 08:18.360
It still needs someone to finish it off,

08:18.360 --> 08:20.580
but when in its invincible 
near-death state,

08:20.580 --> 08:23.930
it reflects all attacks used 
against it, so be careful.

08:23.930 --> 08:26.660
We'll have to wear it down carefully.

08:26.660 --> 08:30.180
Let me. I know its HP.

08:30.180 --> 08:31.480
You do?

08:31.480 --> 08:33.350
I killed one before.

08:33.350 --> 08:35.280
About this much...

08:38.230 --> 08:39.530
Ready now.

08:39.530 --> 08:40.240
Right!

08:43.890 --> 08:45.450
We got it!

08:48.960 --> 08:51.330
This was a victory for teamwork!

08:51.330 --> 08:53.680
That jewel is its drop.

08:53.680 --> 08:57.270
When equipped, it reflects some attacks.

08:57.270 --> 08:59.670
Huh... That sounds pretty cool.

08:59.680 --> 09:02.600
<b>Telulu Level 2</b>

09:02.600 --> 09:06.060
It does seem to be 
reflecting attacks, but...

09:09.320 --> 09:10.450
Carrot!

09:10.450 --> 09:13.090
You defeated it just by standing there!

09:13.090 --> 09:16.240
Hm... I suppose it <i>is</i> convenient, but...

09:16.240 --> 09:19.200
It's faster to attack things myself.

09:19.200 --> 09:21.870
Low-Level's carrots are the best!

09:22.210 --> 09:26.030
I'll just stick with the plan 
and sell this to Erza.

09:33.130 --> 09:35.820
This is the rare drop from Telulu level 7,

09:35.820 --> 09:37.250
the Slime Tear!

09:37.250 --> 09:39.060
Level 7?

09:39.060 --> 09:40.860
Yeah, you know, the guts thing.

09:40.860 --> 09:41.710
Oh...

09:41.710 --> 09:44.110
You'll buy it off me, right?

09:44.420 --> 09:46.960
Yes! Thank you very much!

09:46.960 --> 09:51.660
My shop's rank and trust level 
will go up again, thanks to you!

09:51.660 --> 09:53.450
I'm glad I could be of use.

09:53.690 --> 09:57.380
And here's the 3,000,000 
pilos this item is worth.

09:57.380 --> 09:58.580
That much?!

09:58.820 --> 10:02.920
The price is up right now because 
it's almost harvest festival time.

10:14.120 --> 10:16.790
Excuse me! Please let me join your party!

10:20.260 --> 10:22.070
Please let me...

10:22.070 --> 10:24.320
What, a little kid?

10:29.520 --> 10:32.650
<b>Nihonium Level 5</b>

10:42.600 --> 10:45.920
<i>It's fast! The red skeleton 
is three times as fast!</i>

10:45.920 --> 10:47.090
But...

10:49.200 --> 10:51.120
I'm still faster.

10:53.750 --> 10:57.290
m 0 0 l -42 0 l -46 -4 l -46 -28 l -42 -32 l -28 -32 l -28 -30 l -42 -30 l -44 -28 l -44 -4 l -42 -2 l 0 -2

10:53.750 --> 10:57.290
m 0 0 l -42 0 l -46 -4 l -46 -28 l -42 -32 l -28 -32 l -28 -30 l -42 -30 l -44 -28 l -44 -4 l -42 -2 l 0 -2

10:53.750 --> 10:57.290
Ryota's max MP increased by 1.

10:53.890 --> 10:57.130
<i>Ryota's max MP increased by one.</i>

10:57.130 --> 11:02.240
<i>Oh, so floor 5's drops raise 
your MP, or magic points.</i>

11:02.590 --> 11:07.350
<i>Wait, MP is the energy needed 
to use magic, right?</i>

11:07.690 --> 11:10.780
<i>How do you even learn magic, anyway?</i>

11:13.350 --> 11:15.680
Exactly 3,000,000 pilos...

11:15.680 --> 11:17.260
I can't believe I bought it.

11:17.260 --> 11:22.070
Yes, most people learn 
magic by leveling up,

11:22.070 --> 11:25.110
but you can't level up.

11:25.110 --> 11:28.040
But if you eat this magic fruit,

11:28.040 --> 11:31.200
you can learn a random magic spell.

11:31.200 --> 11:33.570
I had no idea things like this existed...

11:33.570 --> 11:35.530
Eat it now and see what happens!

11:35.530 --> 11:37.140
No, hang on.

11:37.140 --> 11:41.010
There's a reason I went 
outside of town for this.

11:41.010 --> 11:43.350
<i>The odds of this working are fifty-fifty,</i>

11:43.350 --> 11:45.970
<i>but I want to try it.</i>

11:49.340 --> 11:53.260
I see. You let it become a stray
 so it will drop something even better.

12:00.230 --> 12:01.310
Ryota?!

12:01.310 --> 12:03.620
<i>That must be a Metal Ryota!</i>

12:13.010 --> 12:15.790
It's tough! And fast! And strong!

12:16.270 --> 12:20.220
I guess it's a monster that takes on 
80% of the specs of whatever it copies.

12:20.700 --> 12:23.160
Not a monster suited for big gatherings...

12:31.480 --> 12:33.580
It's still just a magic fruit.

12:33.580 --> 12:35.630
No, it's actually not.

12:36.880 --> 12:39.060
Could this mean...

12:39.060 --> 12:42.000
I think... No, I'm sure of it!

12:44.520 --> 12:47.360
Yoda, you've learned magic?!

12:47.360 --> 12:49.140
And two spells?!

12:49.140 --> 12:51.990
Yeah. One is Wind Cutter.

12:51.990 --> 12:54.800
It's a level 1 wind elemental spell.

12:54.800 --> 12:58.620
That's amazing! 
What's the other spell like?

12:58.620 --> 13:00.770
I want to know, too!

13:00.770 --> 13:03.210
It's kind of weird, though.

13:03.490 --> 13:05.560
I'll test it out on those guys.

13:05.560 --> 13:07.560
Okay, do what we always do.

13:07.560 --> 13:08.600
Got it!

13:08.600 --> 13:10.930
Leave it to me! Inferno!

13:15.480 --> 13:16.910
Reservation!

13:19.850 --> 13:21.550
I don't think so!

13:27.150 --> 13:30.560
Wow! It's like I'm Yoda!

13:30.560 --> 13:33.110
You mean that spell was...

13:33.110 --> 13:37.170
Yeah. If it's used in advance on a monster,

13:37.170 --> 13:40.760
my drop rates apply to
 whoever actually defeats it.

13:40.760 --> 13:43.080
So it gives someone drop 
rates equivalent to rank S?

13:43.080 --> 13:45.450
Yeah, but it's not that useful.

13:45.450 --> 13:50.010
It has to be cast on a monster, 
so it only works if I'm there.

13:50.010 --> 13:53.100
That's not true! I'm grateful for it!

13:53.100 --> 13:55.030
Grateful for what?

13:55.030 --> 13:58.970
I think I leveled up after that battle!

13:59.320 --> 14:01.820
Oh, right! When he uses that spell,

14:01.820 --> 14:04.540
someone other than him can 
finish off the monster!

14:04.540 --> 14:06.950
So it helps others level up!

14:06.950 --> 14:10.700
I'm so glad I got a spell 
that'll help my friends!

14:11.140 --> 14:13.520
Let's share the experience from now on,

14:13.520 --> 14:16.060
so everyone can level up together!

14:16.060 --> 14:17.430
Absolutely!

14:17.430 --> 14:18.120
Yes!

14:20.790 --> 14:23.940
<i>Maybe I'll head to Nihonium today...</i>

14:23.940 --> 14:24.460
Huh?

14:24.460 --> 14:25.590
That's...

14:25.870 --> 14:26.930
Erza!

14:26.930 --> 14:28.700
Oh, Ryota!

14:28.700 --> 14:31.210
That's a lot of stuff you're 
carrying. Let me help.

14:31.210 --> 14:35.310
Thank you. I bought too much and 
made things hard for myself.

14:39.260 --> 14:41.240
Thank you for helping!

14:41.240 --> 14:43.010
Well, I'll be on my way, then.

14:43.010 --> 14:44.820
You'll actually let me join?!

14:47.980 --> 14:49.580
Now, run straight in! Got it?!

14:47.990 --> 14:50.490
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

14:47.990 --> 14:50.490
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

14:49.580 --> 14:50.280
Yes, sir!

14:50.280 --> 14:52.710
Too close! And we're too close to floor 7!

14:51.490 --> 14:52.990
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

14:51.490 --> 14:52.990
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

14:52.990 --> 14:58.000
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

14:52.990 --> 14:58.000
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

14:53.280 --> 14:55.000
It wasn't supposed to be like this...

14:55.610 --> 14:58.000
Hey, wait!

14:56.130 --> 14:57.270
Carrot?

14:58.360 --> 15:01.330
Really?! You'll really let me join you?!

15:01.330 --> 15:03.950
Yes. You have potential.

15:03.950 --> 15:06.250
Potential that can only shine in a dungeon!

15:06.250 --> 15:07.750
That guy...

15:07.750 --> 15:09.540
Oh, that girl!

15:09.540 --> 15:13.610
She's been asking around for 
adventurer companions lately.

15:13.610 --> 15:17.820
Her max level is only 2, 
so everyone's turned her down, though.

15:17.820 --> 15:20.690
Come with me! Let's chase 
our dreams in the dungeons—

15:20.690 --> 15:21.740
Hold it.

15:21.980 --> 15:23.470
What do you want?

15:23.470 --> 15:25.640
I want this girl in my party.

15:25.640 --> 15:27.810
Me?! Wh-What?!

15:27.810 --> 15:29.760
I won't let her go.

15:30.650 --> 15:32.490
Not to you!

15:34.590 --> 15:38.500
Wow! You're really going 
to join Ryota's party?

15:38.500 --> 15:39.910
Congratulations!

15:39.910 --> 15:41.980
What an honor to be invited 
into the Ryota Family,

15:41.980 --> 15:44.370
the hottest party in town right now!

15:44.370 --> 15:46.930
You're such a lucky girl!

15:46.930 --> 15:49.420
A l-lucky girl? Me?

15:49.660 --> 15:52.260
Yes! I mean, it's the Ryota Family!

15:52.260 --> 15:55.100
That's the Ryota Sato guy 
everyone's talking about?

15:55.100 --> 15:56.500
The guy from Selen?

15:56.500 --> 15:58.800
I-Is he that big a deal?

15:58.800 --> 16:01.170
Yeah! He's been drawing 
everyone's attention!

16:06.810 --> 16:08.720
Thanks, Erza.

16:08.720 --> 16:09.870
N-Not at all.

16:09.870 --> 16:13.110
Just to make this official... 
Do you want to join my party?

16:13.420 --> 16:14.440
I do!

16:14.440 --> 16:15.990
What's your name?

16:15.990 --> 16:17.230
It's Alice.

16:17.230 --> 16:21.540
Cool. Mine's Sato Ryota. Glad to have you.

16:21.540 --> 16:22.360
Thanks!

16:25.440 --> 16:27.220
All right, first...

16:29.390 --> 16:31.190
Try touching this.

16:31.190 --> 16:32.220
Okay.

16:33.340 --> 16:35.680
<b>"Alice"</b>

16:33.340 --> 16:35.680
<b>Level</b>

16:33.340 --> 16:35.680
<b>Status</b>

16:35.670 --> 16:40.100
<i>Oh, boy... Frankly, the only word 
to describe this is "hopeless."</i>

16:40.100 --> 16:42.780
<i>But considering my own past experiences,</i>

16:42.780 --> 16:45.400
<i>she should be able to 
fight in this dungeon.</i>

16:45.400 --> 16:46.530
What's wrong?

16:46.810 --> 16:49.840
Nothing. You should start 
with some leveling up.

16:49.840 --> 16:51.150
Let's go in.

16:51.150 --> 16:53.320
<b>Nihonium Level 1</b>

16:54.630 --> 16:55.700
What is it?

16:55.700 --> 16:57.980
The air in here really takes me back!

16:57.980 --> 16:59.300
It does?

16:59.300 --> 17:02.830
Yeah! I was born in a dungeon, apparently!

17:02.830 --> 17:03.940
Maybe that's why!

17:03.940 --> 17:04.450
Huh?

17:04.800 --> 17:07.050
My mom said that when she 
was pregnant with me,

17:07.050 --> 17:10.840
I just popped out while she 
was working in a dungeon!

17:10.840 --> 17:12.190
Just popped out?!

17:12.190 --> 17:14.300
Th-That can actually happen?

17:16.540 --> 17:19.820
Anyway, let's go kill some monsters.

17:19.820 --> 17:21.100
So, this way, then!

17:21.100 --> 17:21.640
Huh?

17:21.640 --> 17:25.100
Well, there are lots of 
monsters this way, right?

17:28.050 --> 17:30.020
Wow! Look at them all!

17:30.020 --> 17:33.470
That's pretty amazing. 
You can tell where monsters are?

17:36.240 --> 17:38.280
Try killing these guys.

17:38.280 --> 17:41.430
I'd say they should get you 
to level 2, probably.

17:41.890 --> 17:44.290
Hit them using that rock there.

17:44.290 --> 17:45.740
This one? Got it!

17:50.080 --> 17:51.430
I did it!

17:51.430 --> 17:53.000
Now do the same to the others.

17:53.000 --> 17:53.860
Right!

17:59.810 --> 18:01.440
Did you level up?

18:01.800 --> 18:03.830
Let's step outside and check.

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>"Alice"</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Level</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Status</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Strength</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Vitality</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Intelligence</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Will</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Speed</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Dexterity</b>

18:04.640 --> 18:07.350
<b>Luck</b>

18:07.360 --> 18:10.770
<i>I see. So now she can't 
gain any more levels.</i>

18:10.770 --> 18:11.770
Hey...

18:11.770 --> 18:13.570
Can we go back inside?

18:13.570 --> 18:15.100
Did you lose something?

18:15.100 --> 18:16.700
No, it's not that.

18:16.700 --> 18:20.280
When we were in there earlier, 
Bonesy told me to hurry back.

18:20.280 --> 18:21.790
"Bonesy"?

18:22.080 --> 18:24.750
<b>Nihonium Level 1</b>

18:26.170 --> 18:28.170
That one! Catch it!

18:30.430 --> 18:31.740
What are you gonna do?

18:31.740 --> 18:33.530
It's telling me to defeat it.

18:38.970 --> 18:40.390
What the?!

18:47.170 --> 18:50.230
Yeah! It's nice to have 
you with us, Bonesy!

18:50.230 --> 18:52.130
This is... Bonesy?

18:53.270 --> 18:56.310
Bonesy's gonna fight with us from now on.

18:57.320 --> 18:58.050
Huh?

18:58.400 --> 19:00.240
<b>Telulu Level 1</b>

19:00.230 --> 19:02.650
Go! You can do it!

19:08.970 --> 19:11.260
Good job, Bonesy!

19:11.260 --> 19:13.110
Is that damage going to heal?

19:13.110 --> 19:15.660
Yep. As soon as Bonesy changes back.

19:15.660 --> 19:16.890
That's amazing.

19:16.890 --> 19:18.090
Hey, guess what?

19:18.410 --> 19:21.840
Bonesy is calling me "Big Sis."

19:22.190 --> 19:24.270
Because you were both born in a dungeon?

19:24.270 --> 19:25.780
Oh, yeah!

19:26.240 --> 19:27.760
What now?

19:27.760 --> 19:29.150
Jiggly's calling me.

19:29.400 --> 19:30.720
"Jiggly"?!

19:33.650 --> 19:35.760
This is the one that's calling you?

19:35.760 --> 19:38.470
Yeah. It's telling me to defeat it.

19:40.570 --> 19:43.640
You can do it, Bonesy! I'm rooting for you!

19:50.380 --> 19:52.330
You can do that?!

19:58.910 --> 20:00.940
Good job, Bonesy!

20:00.940 --> 20:03.180
Yeah! It's nice to have 
you with us, Jiggly!

20:03.180 --> 20:05.020
Her naming sense...

20:05.740 --> 20:07.880
Got another new little brother, huh?

20:07.880 --> 20:09.190
No, no!

20:09.420 --> 20:13.240
Bonesy is a girl, so Jiggly's not 
"another" little brother.

20:13.240 --> 20:15.590
You're a girl?!

20:15.980 --> 20:17.420
Hey, Ryota...

20:18.100 --> 20:22.700
Thank you! It's because of you 
that I met Bonesy and Jiggly!

20:22.700 --> 20:25.280
It's not like I did anything 
in particular...

20:25.280 --> 20:26.800
Still, thanks!

20:26.800 --> 20:29.460
Bonesy and Jiggly are 
saying thank you, too!

20:29.770 --> 20:30.980
I'm back.

20:30.980 --> 20:32.360
Hello!

20:32.700 --> 20:34.490
Welcome back, Yoda.

20:34.490 --> 20:36.180
Thanks, Emily.

20:38.670 --> 20:41.170
Did you make that, Emily?

20:41.170 --> 20:44.590
Yes. I made carrot Hamburg steaks today.

20:48.360 --> 20:51.060
I want to eat your carrots all my life!

20:51.060 --> 20:53.160
She just proposed to me.

20:53.160 --> 20:55.350
Th-Th-Th-That's a big problem!

20:55.660 --> 20:57.470
H-How cute!

20:57.760 --> 21:01.190
This is Bonesy, and this is Jiggly.

21:01.830 --> 21:04.010
How can they be so cute?!

21:04.010 --> 21:06.780
Hey, can I snuggle them a little bit?

21:08.260 --> 21:10.190
Oh, they're scared.

21:10.540 --> 21:12.030
Aw...

21:12.030 --> 21:15.060
So you like cute things, Celeste?

21:15.410 --> 21:19.650
I-If you could just... 
let me snuggle you a tiny bit...

21:23.040 --> 21:24.400
Weirdo.

21:28.060 --> 21:30.500
I'm Alice. Nice to meet you all!

21:30.500 --> 21:33.520
I'd like to bring her into 
our party. Is that okay?

21:33.520 --> 21:34.830
No objections!

21:36.430 --> 21:38.050
You like carrots?

21:38.050 --> 21:40.310
Sorry. I'm not a fan of them.

21:40.310 --> 21:42.430
10,000 votes in favor.

21:42.430 --> 21:43.400
You're sure?!

21:43.400 --> 21:45.580
We'll never fight over carrots.

21:46.420 --> 21:47.940
And you, Emily?

21:48.200 --> 21:50.530
Of course, I wholeheartedly agree!

21:50.530 --> 21:56.080
Alice, Bonesy, and Jiggly are 
all part of the Ryota Family!

21:56.080 --> 22:00.120
Yay! Isn't that great, Bonesy and Jiggly?

22:02.420 --> 22:05.330
<i>And that's how we gained another new ally.</i>

22:05.730 --> 22:09.290
<i>It looks like our days are about 
to get even more exciting.</i>
